AUDIO: 'different seed hunt candidates. So, there\'s basically two ways that I\'m using the node. One is I\'m simply doing uh seed hunt. So, I\'m actually doing the full candidates with the full steps. So, you'

[06:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'if I\'m using a turbo Laura, then it\'s obviously something like eight steps or or even less or maybe 10 steps. And uh with the Euler beta uh sampler scheduler setup. And this one what it does is it creates all of the'

[06:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'different seeds right under here and it\'s essentially full generation. And then after that, what I\'ll do in the refiner node is just simply select which seed I want and then it\'s going to'

[06:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'upscale it, not refine, but upscale. I\'ll explain that a little bit later uh because this is actually the biggest change that I\'ve made in this entire workflow. But as I\'ve been testing and playing'

[06:57] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: ComfyUI nodes showing video output settings and file naming conventions.
AUDIO: 'around with this workflow, what I\'ve actually come to realize is that the best way by far to use it is to do the two-stage sampling &gt;&gt; [clears throat]'

[07:10] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '&gt;&gt; with the latent only scouting. So, what this does essentially as the Muse person was explaining as well before is is going to only generate part of your video under these seeds and then'

[07:23] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'after the video generation is done, you essentially see if you put here, let\'s say three steps and your maximum is eight, you\'re only going to see portion of the video being generated. So, you\'re'

[07:36] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'going to see the the motion, Oh, say the draft of the motion, and you are going to get a very mixed audio. So, naturally, because the video has only generated three steps instead of the'

[07:48] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'full eight, you are not going to be able to hear the audio very clearly. It\'s usually muffled and completely like broken. So, I personally don\'t use it to check audio. I use it to check the'

[08:00] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: ComfyUI interface displaying sampling settings and a tooltip for input values.
AUDIO: 'motion and overall that the prompt landed as I wanted. If I\'m doing, let\'s say, generation that requires dialogue, character speaking, or something else, then what I usually do is I crank this up. And if it\'s a very, very big, let\'s'

[08:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
