[09:29] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'doing a refinement, we are doing a pure upscaling. This is This node is based on the custom nodes and workflows of TriDay and sorry, I forgot the other person who'

[09:41] [scene:result]
VISUAL: Multiple video outputs displayed in ComfyUI, demonstrating the effect of different settings.
AUDIO: 'was contributing to the upscaling, but it\'s basically done according to how Minimax wants to be upscaled and the official documentation of it. So, it works fantastically.'

[09:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Uh what it does is it takes the steps automatically from the director node over here. And then it you just have to make sure that your steps for the stages actually match what you have in the'

[10:09] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'director. So, if you\'re doing four steps in your latent scouting, then the second part will be that it will come first complete uh the remaining six steps. So, 10 - 4 is 6. It will complete that for'

[10:21] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'whatever seed you selected. And then afterwards, it will polish and upscale the actual uh seed. So, in this case, if I\'m for example selecting four, what it'

[10:35] [scene:result]
VISUAL: Side-by-side comparison of video outputs, with a "waiting for compile" message in one of the nodes.
AUDIO: 'would do is complete this fourth seed and then it would uh upscale it by 2x. Just make sure that you have selected this uh two values as the two-stage strategy. And when it'

[10:49] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'comes to the polish steps, if you\'re polishing it, then I\'ve been testing anywhere between 1 and 16 steps. I honestly feel that you can do four,'

[11:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'six, or eight steps. 16 is a bit of an overkill. Uh it\'s only you might want to do it if you are actually having a scene with super high uh detail that you want to maintain.'

[11:16] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Or you have a very, very complex scene like what you see here, uh the dance scene. Then you can do uh more steps, but for the most part, eight is actually quite a sweet spot that I\'ve I\'ve been'

